; Double's and Float's primitives, as the Prelude's elided instances will
; use them (D23): the elementary functions, the conversions to Int, which
; raise Overflow past Int's range and Domain for a NaN, round to even at a
; half, the classes, decode and encode; and Float, a Double that binary32
; represents, each result of arithmetic rounded to binary32 by Mid's
; real_to_single, its literals read as binary32 (strtof), so 0.1F is
; 0.100000001490 in twelve digits. Each line is a label and a value; one
; that raises is caught by the harness's try. Written by a script from a
; list of items, each an action of its own, run in order.

